      "content": "What you're feeling doesn't make sense, and it's completely valid to grieve the profound loss of someone you loved. Emotionally, your friend's departure might feel like losing an entire part of your life, leaving you feeling empty and disconnected. It's important to acknowledge these feelings and understand that healing isn't linear and it's okay to not be okay. Consider reaching out to friends, family, or a support group for those who've experienced similar loss. Sharing your experiences with people who understand can provide comfort. Taking time for self-care is crucial during this challenging period. Remember, it's okay to seek professional help if your feelings become overwhelming. Everyone copes differently, and there's no right or wrong way to navigate your grief. You don't have to go through this alone; there are people and resources available to support you through this time.",
